## What’s missing

**The mockup sells a cat stretching halfway across a room. The current game sells a grid with cat faces on it.** Bring back the elastic cat as the main event, and make the café the reason it matters.

- **Composition and depth.** Level 1 leaves a sea of empty grid above three near-identical vertical cats. The carrier floats over a dotted strip, the cushions float beneath it, and the board floats on teal. The target ties these together with window light, contact shadows, raised tiles and an orange cat whose leap leads the eye straight to its carrier. The current café already has that warmth. Gameplay needs to feel like it takes place downstairs in the same house.
- **Character and feedback.** At level 12, repeated front-facing heads and even-width bodies make the cats read as patterned tubes. The mid-flight cat and “Cat-tastic!” compete for attention. At the chain moment, the banner covers the board while the payoff happens at the carrier. Make the cats’ movement and reactions carry the celebration.
- **Hierarchy and motivation.** Thick navy rims give counters, boosters and primary actions similar weight. The win card gives a replay thumbnail more space than the next build. The fail card presents six choices while hiding much of the board. The café offers three purchases before players can see what the house could become. Daily Tasks and Residents feel like inventories, with clipped content at short heights.

**Benchmark.** Color Block Jam makes the destination readable before the move and gives arrival a crisp payoff. Screwdom makes each tap visibly change a physical object. Pixel Flow!, AppMagic’s Q3 2026 hybrid-casual puzzle revenue leader, makes the belt, waiting capacity and resulting action legible. Long Cat Out! can own that same clarity with a distinct payoff: watching a ridiculous length of cat fold into a tiny carrier. [AppMagic’s 2025 report](https://appmagic.rocks/research/casual-report-2025?hl=en) · [Q3 2026 rankings](https://appmagic.rocks/research/Hybridcasual-Puzzles-Q32026/?hl=en) · [Color Block Jam](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/color-block-jam/id6504332779) · [Screwdom](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/screwdom/id6740043080) · [Pixel Flow!](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.loomgames.pixelflow)

## New direction — The sunny boarding room

**Stage.** Set the puzzle on an oak sorting table below the café’s bay window. Use muted sage walls `#689A8D`, honey oak `#BF7948`, ivory tiles `#FFF0D3`, rust binding `#BD582F` and ink `#26334A`. Keep leaves and curtains at the corners. One upper-right light source gives the carriers and cats warm rims and soft down-left shadows. Keep the playable surface evenly lit. Use shallow bevels, subtle tile seams and a stitched rug edge with visible thickness. Reserve the strongest saturation for cats and matching carrier faces.

**Layout and hardware.** At 375×667, budget usable height as **8% HUD / 18% carriers and belt / 9% bench / 54% board / 11% boosters**. Use up to 94% of screen width for the board. Give the active carrier a large molded shell, dark opening, hinged door and count on its sill. Queue two smaller carriers on the same moving belt, with visible end rollers and a stop-click on advance. Set the actual seat count into one wooden bench with recessed cushions. Occupied cats curl up, with color and pattern visible. Pulse the last free seat. Keep a small level tab and pause control above, and three compact booster buttons within thumb reach.

**Cats and first ten seconds.** Draw oversized cheeks, offset ears and expressive paws. Give orange a brave lean, blue a sleepy squint and pink a springy crouch. Build tapered bodies with smooth bends and consistent coat markings. Open directly on three cats, with one glancing at its carrier. At **0–2s**, pulse its exit arrow and the matching carrier rim together. On tap, give it a short crouch, elastic launch, tail snap and soft landing, with a click and haptic as `0/3` becomes `1/3`. Aim for the first carrier departure by **10s** with responsive taps. In level 2, demonstrate waiting through a cushion landing and an automatic hop when the matching carrier arrives. Put chain counts beside the carrier.

**Results.** Win on a warm cream card with a resident leaning over the rim, a star flying into the next build meter, and one dominant **Build** or **Next** action. Move sharing behind a small icon. On fail, keep the full bench visible above a short sheet. Point to the blocked cat and show “Bench full. Mint carrier two away.” Lead with **Take back** when free, keep **Retry** visible, and group the other rescues under **More options**.

**House and return loop.** Give the active cutaway floor roughly 60% of hub height. Keep Play pinned and show one build with its visible consequence. The pastry display brings Mochi downstairs. Completing the ground floor raises the walls of the upstairs nap loft, followed by a rooftop greenhouse. Use a floor selector and zoom between house and room. Fit every menu at **375×667 without scrolling**, with 44 px targets. Use Login/Tasks tabs, paged 2×2 resident cards and paged shop offers. Give players a rotating resident request daily, a themed Cat Show puzzle weekly and a new floor chapter monthly. Let event rewards furnish the house.

**Asset brief.** Layered boarding room, modular tile/rug kit, carrier rig with color and pattern variants, belt and bench states, deformable cat rigs with launch/curl/land poses, shared UI components, stackable floor shells, staged furniture, resident animations and a short sound/haptic set.
